            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0583" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">391.51/562: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-11T14:00:00+03:25">March 11, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>285. Another currency crisis has been narrowly avoided by two factors. First,
                    arrival by air from England of 250,000,000 rials of new currency local supply
                    said to be exhausted and second, British approval of the second alternative
                    given in my telegram 223, March 1st, which will permit immediate delivery of
                    British gold to Iran Government and the issue without delay of new currency
                    against sales of sterling.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
